  "review": [
    {
      "id": 4056740876,
      "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Treat escaped direct eval as an ambiguity barrier**\n\nIn a CommonJS script such as `\\u0065val(\"var require = custom\"); require(\"./x\")`, the Unicode escape denotes the identifier `eval` and therefore has direct-eval semantics, but this raw-text equality check does not recognize it. Unlike escaped `require` bindings handled below, `ambiguous` remains false, so the extractor incorrectly emits an observed dependency for a call whose `require` binding may have been replaced; decode this identifier or conservatively treat escaped `eval` spellings as a barrier.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.",
      "path": "src/diffwitness/structure_javascript.py",
      "commit_id": "e56a5a7884072ea51f29d9475235fd942f70c992"
    }
  ]
